{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → acc 0.485, F1 0.464), so evidence is extremely sparse. The most critical open question for a multimodal cellular profiling study is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest single-axis comparison: it mirrors config_001's simplicity (single profile, no aggregation, no fusion) while swapping the modality. This establishes the image-only baseline, which is essential before interpreting any multimodal result—without it, we cannot tell whether a multimodal configuration is genuinely benefiting from fusion or simply performing at the RNA-only level. It also isolates the effect of the image encoder (ResNet50) without confounding from aggregation or fusion choices. Under a tight budget, securing both unimodal baselines before testing fusion is the highest-information-per-experiment strategy."
}

